--TEST--
`Filter::parse` reads text as a filter's structure, so a `tainted` text does not compile, and that includes the `tainted` text `toString` returns — ADR 0278 § 6, `rule:core-classes/ldap-filter-is-a-value` and `rule:security/unclassified-parameter-refuses-tainted`
--FILE--
<?nvs
tainted string $text = "(cn=Ann)";
var $fromInput = Core\Ldap\Filter::parse($text);
var $fromLog = Core\Ldap\Filter::parse(Core\Ldap\Filter::present("cn")->toString());
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:3:42
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:4:40
%A
